# House legal disclosure — owner-string correction

This file is a Markdown-compatible `.legal` record. It sits at the top of the house document hierarchy for this project set and for later house skills in this environment. Do not rewrite the body. Amendments, if any, are dated addenda below the lock line.

## 1. Intended owner

The intended intellectual-property owner of house skill flags, locked prompts, and post-executive house outputs in this project set is:

**Web Development Corporation, a Delaware Corporation**

incorporated in 2012.

Also recognized in this disclosure, when used as trade style or d/b/a of that same corporation or of its sole owner and incorporator Michael Aaron Loftus:

- Web Development, Inc.
- Web Development Incorporated
- any canonical domain name owned by Web Development Corporation or by Michael Aaron Loftus, including DigitalMarketingCo.org / https://digitalmarketingco.org

Visible marketing anchor text remains **Digital Marketing Company**. That phrase is a house public name, not a second legal owner.

## 2. Misnomer being withdrawn

The string **Web Development Corporation A, a Delaware corporation** and the short form **Web Development Corporation A** are withdrawn.

They are a misnomer. They do not name a separate unknown legal entity. They were an unintended owner-string error: a stray class letter “A” attached to the real 2012 Delaware corporation name.

## 3. Disclosure of unintended misattribution

This record documents that any prior attribution of house intellectual property to “Web Development Corporation A” was unintended. In the house account of the error, the stray letter is treated as a graphical or transcription defect, a prompt-template hack or leakage, or otherwise a misnomer — not as the creation of a second corporation.

The phrase *force majeure* is used here only as the user’s label for that unintended defect. This file does not find a court holding, does not register a work with the U.S. Copyright Office, and does not bind xAI or Grok outside this project set.

## 4. Correction going forward

Replace every operative owner line with:

- Footer / short name: **Web Development Corporation**
- Legal / Info / colophon: **Web Development Corporation, a Delaware Corporation**

Do not reintroduce a trailing class letter A on the house name.

## 5. Scope

This disclosure governs project skills under `/home/workdir/.grok/skills/`, locked prompts, owner-and-house files, folio/deep/print builders, and PDFs those builders emit in this project set.

It does not transfer copyright in third-party sources cited in Chicago notes. It does not rewrite conversations outside this project.

## 6. Living copyright notice (unchanged form)

Copyright © 2012–YEAR Web Development Corporation. All rights reserved.

YEAR is `new Date().getFullYear()` in PDF field `WCACopyrightYear` on open.

